ALL NODES DISTANCE K IN BINARY TREE
🟢 Problem Statement

Given:

Root of a Binary Tree

A target node

An integer K

Return all nodes that are exactly distance K away from target node.

Distance = number of edges.

🔎 Example
Tree:

        3
       / \
      5   1
     / \  / \
    6  2 0   8
      / \
     7   4

Target = 5
K = 2

Output:
[7,4,1]

🧠 Explanation

Distance 1 from 5 → {6,2,3}
Distance 2 from 5 → {7,4,1}

🟢 Why This Question is Tricky?

Binary Tree normally:

Can move downward

Cannot move upward

But distance K might require:

Going up to parent

Then to sibling subtree

So problem becomes a Graph problem.

🟢 Key Idea

Convert Binary Tree into an Undirected Graph

Each node connects:

Left child

Right child

Parent

Then perform BFS from target node until distance K.

🟢 Algorithm Steps
Step 1: Build Parent Map

Use DFS to store:

child → parent

Step 2: BFS from Target

Use:

Queue

Visited Set

Start from target.

For each BFS level:

Increase distance

Stop when distance == K

Return all nodes at that level

🟢 Java Code
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    Map<TreeNode, TreeNode> parentMap = new HashMap<>();

    public List<Integer> distanceK(TreeNode root, TreeNode target, int k) {

        buildParentMap(root, null);

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        Set<TreeNode> visited = new HashSet<>();

        queue.offer(target);
        visited.add(target);

        int distance = 0;

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            int size = queue.size();

            if (distance == k) {
                List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
                for (TreeNode node : queue) {
                    result.add(node.val);
                }
                return result;
            }

            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {

                TreeNode current = queue.poll();

                // left child
                if (current.left != null && !visited.contains(current.left)) {
                    queue.offer(current.left);
                    visited.add(current.left);
                }

                // right child
                if (current.right != null && !visited.contains(current.right)) {
                    queue.offer(current.right);
                    visited.add(current.right);
                }

                // parent
                TreeNode parent = parentMap.get(current);
                if (parent != null && !visited.contains(parent)) {
                    queue.offer(parent);
                    visited.add(parent);
                }
            }

            distance++;
        }

        return new ArrayList<>();
    }

    private void buildParentMap(TreeNode node, TreeNode parent) {

        if (node == null) return;

        parentMap.put(node, parent);

        buildParentMap(node.left, node);
        buildParentMap(node.right, node);
    }
}

